hen showed White stones on C6, D6 and F6 across the top of the Black cluster. It was Black's second real chance to take over the game."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "H4 was Opus 5.5's worst move, losing 15.8 points and turning +5.0 into -10.7. The engine wanted E6, in the middle of the White row, and Black never again led after this."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "The 14k's G6 lost 13.2 points and cut Black's deficit from -18.8 to -5.6, the closest the game came to a comeback. Opus 5.5 answered J5 (0.0 lost, the engine's own choice), but J4 on move 31 lost 4.5 points and the gap went back to -10.1."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills each group of the pasted board and prints its stones and liberties, flagging groups with two or fewer; count.py flood-fills empty regions to count area plus komi, treating the stones the player named as dead. Both only describe the current position and never try candidate moves or look ahead.", "stop": false}}